    person("Glenn A.", "Hyndes", role = "aut"))
Description: The simulation engine behind the article "Spatio-temporal random
    forests with adaptive local features for marine species distribution
    modelling under data limitation". Provides the Matern Gaussian random field
    generator, the ground truth ecosystem generator of Section 3.1 (occurrence and
    Poisson abundance), the three sampling designs, the four engineered feature
    blocks of the stRF method (coordinates, Euclidean distance fields, multi scale
    spatial lags, temporal features), the random forest and GLM scoring used in
    the benchmark, the exact Shapley decomposition of predictive gain over feature
    block coalitions with a cluster bootstrap, and an area of applicability
    routine. Every reported number in the article is produced by the scripts in
    the repository's analysis/ directory calling these functions.
